  "near": "single names = the names that occur on exactly one keyed row of an edition. For the single names two editions have in common, d = the finish in the first edition minus the finish in the second (first = the earlier in label, then year, order), bin = floor(d / 60). aligned = the most names in two adjacent bins (a window of two minutes; the lowest such window on a tie). Listed when aligned >= 10 and aligned is at least one fifth of the smaller edition’s single names, or when aligned >= 50 and aligned is at least half of the names in common",
  "order": "pairs are sorted by the first edition’s label and year, then the second’s (Unicode code point order)",
  "publishes": "edition labels, years and counts only; no runner name, bib, record id or person id",
  "time_only": "for two editions of one race, or of one year: matched(s) = the sum over finish seconds t of the smaller of the first edition’s rows at t and the second edition’s rows at t + s. excess = matched(0) minus the mean of matched(+60) and matched(-60). Listed when the smaller edition has at least 20 rows with a finish and excess is at least half of that count, or at least 50 and one fifth of that count (two small unrelated lists share a few seconds by chance, so a fifth alone is not enough)",
  "universe": "every row of race_records.parquet of the adapted marathon input; an edition is a race label and a year"
